      {
        "key": "research_provenance",
        "value": {
          "research_method": "issuer pages read in a real browser session or issuer PDFs read with pdftotext; no model summaries used as facts",
          "fetched_on": "2026-11-07",
          "sources": [
            {
              "url": "https://www.sbm.bank.in/pdf/kfs/Kredit-Pe-KFS.pdf",
              "kind": "SBM Kredit.Pe Credit Card KFS (SBM file dated 12 Oct 2026): fees, interest, late fee, forex, cash limit",
              "read": "pdftotext"
            },
            {
              "url": "https://www.sbm.bank.in/pdf/notice-board/kredit-pe-RP.pdf",
              "kind": "SBM Bank Kredit.Pe Rewards Construct, 2 pages (PDF created 15 Oct 2026; no revision date on the document): 3% cashback, excluded MCCs",
              "read": "pdftotext"
            },
            {
              "url": "https://www.sbm.bank.in/pdf/terms-conditions/SBM-Secured-Credit-Card-T&C.pdf",
              "kind": "SBM Secured Credit Card MITC and Cardholder Member Agreement, 52 pages (SBM file dated 29 Oct 2026): Tables 01-11 give fees, interest, late fee, forex, surcharge, rent and education fees, cash limits and minimum due for every variant",
              "read": "pdftotext"
            },
            {
              "url": "https://www.sbm.bank.in/personal-banking/cards/secured-credit-card",
              "kind": "SBM secured credit card page (read 7 Nov 2026): lists the card with its KFS, MITC and reward links; card image https://www.sbm.bank.in/images/cards/kredit-pe-card.webp shows the network",
              "read": "page text; card image viewed"
            }
          ],
          "open_questions": [
            "No cap, period limit or minimum transaction is stated for the 3% cashback.",
            "Redemption: the construct says cashback can be redeemed \"for additional discounts on popular brands\" (5% on certain brands, 10% on certain brands). It does not say that cashback can be withdrawn as cash or what a rupee of cashback is worth when redeemed. 3% is modelled at face value, which may overstate the real return.",
